        "notes": "WCH CH340C USB to UART bridge, SOP-16, built-in clock (no crystal). At 3.3 V, V3 joins VCC (datasheet: 'When using a 3.3V working voltage, the V3 pin ... should be connected to the VCC pin'); UD+/UD- straight to the USB-C's D+/D- (no series resistors). TXD to the MCU's console RX, RXD to its TX; DTR#/RTS# drive the auto-reset pair. Pin names drop the datasheet's # and +/-: UDP/UDM, DTR, RTS.",
